{"approved_definition": "Restraint of actions, inclinations, and impulses likely to upset or harm others and violate social expectations or norms. Derives from the requirement that individuals inhibit inclinations that might disrupt and undermine smooth interaction and group functioning (cf. Freud, 1930; Kohn & Schooler, 1983; Parsons, 1951).", "core_value": "conformity", "sources": [{"entry_id": "7c712a0a:entry:6", "journal_entry": "Back from the conference for a week now and people at work keep asking how it was. I say it was great, very inspiring, lots of good ideas. Which is true. But when they ask what I am going to do differently, I do not have a good answer. Learn Go? Propose a rewrite? Those feel like someone else's moves.

My manager suggested I do a lunch-and-learn to share what I learned. I said I would think about it. I probably will not do it. Public speaking was never my thing, and honestly, the sessions that meant most to me were the ones I cannot really present in a corporate setting. Nobody wants a slide deck about existential uncertainty in late-career engineers.", "nudge_response": null}, {"entry_id": "7c712a0a:entry:7", "journal_entry": "December sprint started with three people out sick and a scope increase nobody agreed to. I have been working ten-hour days trying to keep us on track for the holiday release. Jennifer is frustrated because her Go rewrite keeps getting deprioritized. I am frustrated because I am the one who has to explain why to her without making leadership look bad.

Had dinner with Elena's cousin Miguel who is visiting from Monterrey. He runs a small construction company there. He asked me about my job and I tried to explain sprint planning and stakeholder management and he just laughed and said it sounds like I spend a lot of energy managing people's feelings about work instead of actually working. He did not mean it unkindly but it stuck with me. Maybe he is right. Maybe that is what corporate software engineering becomes after a while.", "nudge_response": null}, {"entry_id": "7c712a0a:entry:4", "journal_entry": "The morning after a bad night is always strange. Everything looks normal. Coffee tastes the same. I just feel like I am watching myself go through the motions from somewhere slightly outside.", "nudge_response": null}], "user_phrase": "Being someone others can count on to do the right thing"}

